Error [E1102]: `h` can't cross into a task because `Holder` isn't sendable
  --> tests/ui/task_detach_unsound.jet:8:22
    |
  8 |     t :: tasks.spawn(() => h)
    |                      ^^^^^^^
 Why: `Holder` contains `name`, which is a `ref` field; tasks and channels move owned values between threads
 Fix: give the task plain owned data, or remove the shared-view field before spawning

Error [E1102]: this task returns `Holder`, which isn't sendable
  --> tests/ui/task_detach_unsound.jet:8:22
    |
  8 |     t :: tasks.spawn(() => h)
    |                      ^^^^^^^
 Why: `Holder` contains `name`, which is a `ref` field; tasks and channels move owned values between threads
 Fix: give the task plain owned data, or remove the shared-view field before spawning

Error [E1103]: can't detach task `t` — it captured a value that can't cross a thread boundary
  --> tests/ui/task_detach_unsound.jet:9:7
    |
  9 |     t.detach()
    |       ^^^^^^
 Why: a detached task runs unsupervised; it must only hold values it owns cleanly
 Fix: fix the E1102 error at the spawn site first, then `.detach()` is safe
